  Answer #3

    Answer: Five (and not seven as one might believe)
    
    Why?
    We are tempted to believe that there should be seven faces in all since
    we started with 9 faces in all and lost two when we glued the pyramids
    together. However, there are two pairs of faces which are not glued
    together but are aligned in the same plane and so give give just one face
    each when the solids are glued together. Thus we end up with two faces
    less than expected.
    
      WINNER: Illumineaux
